From c41778da05be5cfb6648cdda0279d7a9643c44b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:49:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] ad5x: Boot rules: state in ota, 6.6, 7.3 or the stock
 kernel, checked fallback

The start was decided in the environment: boot_pending set before each
start of the main OS, and still set at the next one meant the recovery
OS at once, with the flag on slot A, the stock kernel read as a fixed
5 MiB (Kiln's 6.6 is about 5.9 MiB), slot A started unchecked, only 6.6
from rootfs2, and the watchdog left running for 300 s into a kernel and
userspace that don't feed it.

Decide in C instead (bootlogic.c, plain C so the build host can test
it), from what U-Boot reads without writing a filesystem:

- the boot flag; a state sector (unconfirmed starts of the main OS and
  the kernel of the last one) and a records sector (failed releases, the
  reason for the last fallback), text with a CRC32 in "ota" at 0x90000
  and 0x90200; a sector that doesn't parse counts as empty;
- /data (ext4, read only): kernel/mainline, kernel/failed,
  kernel/failed-mainline, install/recovery.squashfs, as S00ad5x-kernel
  keeps them;
- rootfs2 (SquashFS): the 6.6 and 7.3 kernels and their releases;
- slot A: p1 a Linux uImage (not a U-Boot) with good header and data
  CRCs, read whole by its header's length, and p2 starting with "hsqs".

The rules follow S00ad5x-kernel's: 7.3 when chosen and not failed, else
6.6, else the stock kernel; one unfinished 7.3 start records its release
and goes on to 6.6, two unfinished starts of 6.6 (one on the first start
after an install) record its release and go on to the stock kernel; two
of the stock kernel, or no kernel at all, fall back to the recovery OS:
"ota:kernel" written over the flag's first bytes as Linux writes it, the
state cleared, the reason recorded. A start of the recovery OS clears
the state too. A slot A that isn't startable is never started: the main
OS again (the flag pointed back at slot B), or the prompt when nothing
can start. A record naming another release than the one installed is
dropped. Counts saturate.

The kernels start with the stock SPL's command line, root=/dev/mmcblk0p2
or p4, ad5x.uboot=1, and for 6.6/7.3 "ad5x.kernel=own panic=10
loglevel=5" plus /data/ad5x/kernel/cmdline-extra, as S00 adds them.

Watchdog: armed for 120 s from board_early_init_f, so a hang in U-Boot
resets the board (the SPL then sees "U-Boot up" in the scratch pad and
skips it); stopped just before the jump (board_preboot_os), as both SPLs
leave it, because neither kernel's driver knows it runs, nothing would
feed it before userspace and poweroff wouldn't stop it. wdt_os=SECONDS
opts in. A key within ad5x_delay seconds gives the prompt with the
watchdog off; so does a start that fails. ad5x_boot -n shows what would
be started and why. Before any write, the GPT must match the stock
SPL's table. ad5x_flag writes only the flag's bytes, not the sector.

The environment holds settings only and is reset to the build's when it
comes from another build.
