 /*
  * Flashforge Adventurer 5X (Ingenic X2600)
+ *
+ * U-Boot proper: started by Kiln's SPL from eMMC 0xA400, or wrapped as a
+ * uImage from a kernel slot by either SPL. It starts the main OS (slot B)
+ * with the kernel /data/ad5x/kernel/mainline and the failure records ask
+ * for, or the recovery OS (slot A), by the rules in bootlogic.c. It reads
+ * /data (ext4) and rootfs2 (SquashFS) and never writes a filesystem; what
+ * it writes is in the "ota" partition: the boot flag (bytes 0-11, only
+ * when it falls back or slot A isn't startable), its state and records
+ * (512-byte sectors at 0x90000 and 0x90200) and its environment (512 KiB
+ * and 544 KiB).
